    <office:text>
      <text:p text:style-name="Title">Interior design scope of work template</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Meta">Blank editable template</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Meta">OpenLintel • Educational planning resource • September 26, 2026</text:p>
      <text:p>Illustrative teaching extension of The Window Room; not a client record, supplier quote, site survey, or construction-ready document. Pending professional review.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="RustHeading">How to use</text:p>
      <text:p>Use this as a planning attachment to a project discussion. Agree responsible parties and interfaces explicitly; this document contains no legal terms and does not replace a project agreement. Review each exclusion for an unresolved interface; name the needed provider without inventing an appointment.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•    Name the deliverable and its intended use.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•    Assign responsibility at each handoff, including work provided by others.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•    Record changes against the agreed baseline rather than overwriting it.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="RustHeading">Review before use</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•    An exclusion is not a complete plan unless someone owns the interface.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•    A concept drawing is not automatically a construction document.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•    A task list without an agreed boundary does not define scope.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="LastBody">Replace illustrative information with verified project records. No approval, legal agreement, or construction readiness is represented. Keep completed client documents in your own secure system.</text:p>

      <text:p text:style-name="PageStart">Your project</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FirstSectionHeading">Project boundary</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionBody">Name included rooms and distinguish work areas from adjacent coordination areas.</text:p>
      <text:p>[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionHeading">Discovery and brief</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionBody">List the information to gather and the output to review.</text:p>
      <text:p>[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionHeading">Concept development</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionBody">State what will be compared and what happens after selection.</text:p>
      <text:p>[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionHeading">Drawings and schedules</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionBody">Specify document names, intended use, and level of detail.</text:p>
      <text:p>[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionHeading">Responsibilities</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionBody">Record who provides measurements, approves selections, coordinates specialists, and places orders. Leave unresolved roles explicit.</text:p>
      <text:p>[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionHeading">Review checkpoints</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionBody">Define when feedback is required and who consolidates it. Put revision allowances in the separately agreed scope.</text:p>
      <text:p>[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionHeading">Exclusions and interfaces</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionBody">List omitted services and information you must receive from others.</text:p>
      <text:p>[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>

      <text:p text:style-name="PageStart">Change record</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="SectionBody">Document a requested change and its potential effect before altering the baseline.</text:p>
      <text:p>[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
